    "result_text": "The full suite (one test class, `AcceptanceTest`) is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `GOLD` membership tier rule: an owner is `GOLD` when its household (owners sharing the same `householdId` \u2014 i.e. same normalized last name + address) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing `SILVER`/`BRONZE` rules still apply.\n\nBecause `membershipTier` is derived at response-mapping time and `GET /api/owners/{id}` re-loads the owner from the DB, the household size has to be persisted at create time (exactly like the existing `namesakeCount`). Changes:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column; **`hsqldb/data.sql`** seed rows got an extra `NULL` to match (hsqldb is the test DB and uses positional inserts).\n- **`CountHouseholdMembers.java`** (new) \u2014 pipeline step following the `CountNamesakes` pattern: counts existing owners sharing the same `Household.id`, stores `existing + 1` as the household size. Runs before `SaveOwner` so the new owner isn't double-counted.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `namesakes`, before `bulkSignup`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`MembershipTier.of(...)`** \u2014 now takes `householdSize` first and returns `GOLD` when it's \u2265 3, else the prior logic.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 passes `owner.getHouseholdSize()` into the tier expression.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document `GOLD`.\n\nThe provided acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passes, and the full test suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
